#. Tag: title
#: getkde.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting &kde;"
msgstr " "

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I get &kde;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The easiest way to get &kde; is to install a &Linux; distribution or another "
"UNIX-like OS that ships with &kde;. You can find an up-to-date list of "
"distributions that ship with &kde; <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.kde.org/download/distributions.php\">here</ulink>"
". For alternative methods of trying &kde; that do not require you to be running "
"&Linux;, please see <ulink url=\"http://kde.org/try_kde\">Try &kde;</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main distribution site for &kde; is <ulink url=\"ftp://ftp.kde.org/\">"
"ftp.kde.org</ulink>. However, this site is often under heavy load, so you might "
"prefer to use <ulink url=\"http://download.kde.org/\">download.kde.org</ulink> "
"which automatically redirects you to the mirror nearest to you. You can also "
"have a look at the list of <ulink url=\"http://www.kde.org/ftpmirrors.html\"> "
"&kde; mirror sites</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is the current version?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "Currently, the latest stable version is 3.5.5"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <ulink url=\"http://www.kde.org/info/3.5.5.php\">"
"&kde; 3.5.5 Info Page</ulink> contains a lot of information specific to this "
"release."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I find &kde; snapshots?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can get the latest snapshots from <ulink "
"url=\"ftp://ftp.kde.org/pub/kde/unstable/snapshots\">"
"ftp://ftp.kde.org/pub/kde/unstable/snapshots</ulink>"
". You might also want to consider setting up your own <acronym>SVN</acronym> "
"client in order to maintain the latest snapshot at all times. Please refer to "
"<ulink url=\"http://developer.kde.org/source/anonsvn.html\">Anonymous <acronym>"
"SVN</acronym> and &kde;</ulink> for further information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I get &Qt;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&Qt; is a product of the Norwegian company Trolltech. You can always get the "
"latest &Qt; version from their <ulink url=\"ftp://ftp.trolltech.com\">"
"&FTP; server</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getkde.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"And with most up-to-date &Linux; distributions, &Qt; is already included. "
"Please see <xref linkend=\"prerequisites\"/> for the version of &Qt; you need."
msgstr ""

